+# Submitted-program construct-to-semantics map
+
+The submitted MPY term uses `Module`, `FuncDef`, `Params`, statement/argument
+list units, `Assign`, `Name`, `ListExpr`, `While`, `Compare`, `CmpOp`, `If`,
+`BinOp`, `Int`, `Expr`, `Call`, `Attribute`, and `Return`. Their declarations
+are in `reference-semantics/semantics/syntax.k` lines 9–61, with left-to-right
+evaluation generated by `[strict]`/`[seqstrict]` where declared and explicit
+contexts for `Compare` in `operators.k` lines 14–17.
+
+| Program behavior | Fixed supplied-semantics source |
+|---|---|
+| Module load and statement sequencing | `core.k:124-127` |
+| Function definition and exact closure creation | `functions.k:14-16` |
+| Function lookup, call, frame allocation, parameter binding | `core.k:130-181`; `call.k:18-21,69-75`; `functions.k:62-66` |
+| Integer and list literals; fresh list allocation | `core.k:117-121,193-196`; `list.k:12-15` |
+| Local assignment | `controls.k:8-18` |
+| Name lookup through local/module/builtin scopes | `core.k:129-181` |
+| `%`, `==`, `!=`, `*`, `+`, and `//` over integers | `operators.k:10-17`; `int.k:9-27` |
+| `if` branch selection | `controls.k:50-54` |
+| `while` condition, body, and loop-back continuation | `controls.k:65-85` |
+| Attribute/call evaluation | `call.k:15-32`; `core.k:183-191` |
+| In-place `list.append` and sequence concatenation | `list.k:17-20,52-55` |
+| Expression-statement result discard | `controls.k:46-48` |
+| Builtin `sorted` lookup and first-argument dereference | `core.k:156-181`; `call.k:34-46` |
+| `sorted(list)` result allocation | `sort.k:14-37`; symbolic value is opaque `sortVS`, LLVM uses guarded insertion sort |
+| Return, abrupt body discard, frame pop, and result restoration | `functions.k:77-90` |
+
+`verification.k:8-22` expands the reviewer-facing `#getOddCollatz(N)` symbol to
+the exact normalized MPY module plus `Call(Name("get_odd_collatz"), Int(N))`.
+It is an abbreviation and does not replace any operation in the function body.
+
+The proof-local `collatzResult` equations at `verification.k:28-41` are
+guard-disjoint and follow the same recurrence, but they are dead with respect
+to the submitted theorem: `spec.k` contains zero occurrences of
+`collatzResult`.
